{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>From without one observing.</b> Its meaning is: from understanding. Similar to it: \"and they set [it] and understand\" (Isaiah 41:20 — וישימו וישכילו)." "<b>They are crushed.</b> From כתית. The sense is like: \"in the morning it flourishes and fades\" (Psalm 90:6 — בבקר יציץ וחלף)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The lemma corresponds to מבלי משים in Job 4:20; Ibn Ezra reads משים as cognate with understanding/intellect.", 1 "Hebrew lemma יוכתו is parsed as from the root כתת; comparison to Psalm 90:6 is by way of illustrating the form or the sense of passing away."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:46.932569144Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}